{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-steer-busy-merged-system-reminder",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 6 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 6/L6): steer_session called against a child that is definitionally still busy (spawn_session registers the child as inFlight synchronously, and its only call is gated open — never released until after the steer already happened, so busy-ness is guaranteed by construction, not a race) queues the raw text; it surfaces merged into a single <system-reminder>...</system-reminder> user message, drained at the top of the child's next iteration (its second, since its first tool_calls response already required one). Sentinel __SUB__ (mirrors the Evaluator's own harness) resolves the just-spawned child's real sub_id for the steer_session call. The parent makes an extra probe tool call AFTER steering and BEFORE opening the child's gate specifically to give the child's own post-release processing (parse tool_calls, dispatch read_file, drain the steer inbox, build iteration 2) a full extra real HTTP round trip of headroom before the parent's own turn can finish and teardown can fire — without it, this collapses into the exact same scheduler-dependent race documented in section O (candidate interrupts before the child's second iteration, oracle does not). KNOWN LIMIT (declared, not a gap to fix): events.requests is excluded from bilateral comparisons — the child's FIRST request's arrival position relative to the parent's is scheduler-dependent (measured stable-but-different: always index 1 on the candidate, always index 2 on the oracle, across repeated runs), the same class of non-discriminable-by-scheduling property as section O. The child's SECOND request (carrying the merged reminder) lands at a stable index on both sides once construction removes the interrupt race, so the reminder's exact content is still verified below via a targeted, side-scoped expectation at that fixed pointer.",
  "argv": [
    "chat",
    "SCEN:parent spawn a child and steer it while busy",
    "--json",
    "--provider",
    "ollama",
    "--model",
    "stub-coder:1b"
  ],
